  <section class="sec" id="faq" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> FAQ</span>
        <h2>Remote vs in-house questions, answered.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>How much cheaper is a remote team member than an in-house hire? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">For most administrative, support, finance, and marketing roles, a dedicated remote professional costs 40 to 65 percent less than the fully loaded cost of an equivalent US in-house hire, once payroll taxes, benefits, recruiting, and equipment are included on the in-house side.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What is loaded cost and why does it matter? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">Loaded cost is salary plus everything the employer pays on top: payroll taxes, insurance, retirement, recruiting, equipment, and workspace. US data puts benefits alone at roughly 38 to 40 percent of wages, so comparing salary to a remote rate understates the real gap.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Do I lose control with a remote professional? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">No. A dedicated professional works only for your business, on your hours, inside your systems, reporting to you. The difference from an in-house hire is who handles employment and payroll, not who directs the work.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Which roles should stay in-house? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">Roles needing physical presence, hands-on equipment, in-person client delivery, or location-bound security clearance. Most back-office, support, finance operations, and marketing execution roles work well remotely.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What if the remote hire does not work out? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">Every Remote Team Partners placement carries a replacement guarantee. If the professional is not the right fit, we recruit and onboard a replacement at no additional recruiting cost.</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

